TITLE = "Iunonis ira. Aeolus"
TITLE_EN = "Juno's Anger and the Storm — Aeneid I.1–101"
PART = "Juno's Anger and the Storm (I.1–101)"
ABOUT = ("The opening of the Aeneid. Virgil names his subject — war, and a man driven by fate from Troy to Italy to found the line that leads to Rome — and asks the Muse why the queen of the gods hated so good a man. Then the story begins, in the middle: the Trojans are leaving Sicily, seven years after Troy fell, when Juno, nursing her grievances, goes to Aeolus, keeper of the winds, and bribes him with a nymph to wreck their fleet. "
         "The storm breaks, and Aeneas, named for the first time ninety-two lines in, wishes he had died fighting at Troy. "
         "Virgil writes in dactylic hexameter, the metre of Homer, and he writes against Homer throughout: the storm, the hero's despair and the keeper of the winds all come from the Odyssey, retold for Rome.")
